{"event_id":"EVT-000056","timestamp_utc":"2026-08-29T09:21:54.931Z","session_id":"SESSION-BATCH-20260829T055713815378Z","run_id":"RUN-IMO-120-20260829T092009364337Z","requirement_id":"IMO-120","event_type":"validator_feedback_possible_reversal","iteration":2,"prior_feedback_history":["Repair the conditional logic and semantic coverage. Do not require the redundant nltl:arcticWaters applicability field; operatingArea and foodWasteDischargeToSea already determine applicability. When operatingArea is Arctic_waters and foodWasteDischargeToSea is true, require distanceToNearestLandIceShelfOrFastIce >= 12 MI_N and explicitly encode the distinct ice-area condition: nearbyIceConcentration must be compared as exceeding one tenth (with the declared unit) and distanceFromAreaWithIceConcentrationAboveOneTenth must be recorded and paired with that condition. The current branches only check presence of nearbyIceConcentration, iceConcentration, and the second distance and therefore permit missing comparison/relationship semantics; also avoid a branch formulation that can pass by omitting or inadequately constraining applicability evidence."],"current_feedback":"Repair the conditional logic before freezing. The first sh:or branch matches merely on Arctic_waters plus foodWasteDischargeToSea=true and therefore permits the applicable case to pass without enforcing any distance or ice conditions; remove it or replace it with a genuine non-applicable alternative so applicable ships must satisfy every constraint. Preserve the existing applicability inputs without adding arcticWaters. In the applicable branch retain distanceToNearestLandIceShelfOrFastIce >= 12 MI_N, nearbyIceConcentration > 0.1 with unit:UNITLESS, and the recorded distanceFromAreaWithIceConcentrationAboveOneTenth in MI_N, with those two ice-area values on the same supplied case/ship node as the explicit pairing. Remove the needless presence-only iceConcentration constraint, since it is not a required result or independently constrained obligation here.","blocking":false,"semantic_attempt_consumed":false}
